    <string name="wi_title">Word Impostor</string>
    <string name="wi_tagline">One word. A room full of suspicion.</string>
    <string name="wi_subtitle">3–12 players · Questions, votes, secrets</string>
    <string name="wi_open">Join the conversation</string>
    <string name="wi_rules">Ordinary players share a secret word. Impostors know their teammates, never the word. Everyone asks once and answers once, then talks freely. The host opens voting. Each player secretly votes for someone else; totals appear only after all vote. The top K suspects must identify all K impostors, without a tie at the cutoff, for every ordinary player to earn a point. Each impostor then guesses individually from five same-topic choices and earns one point for a correct answer. Both teams can score. Keep word screens private.</string>
